('6b3e2964-deda-50ba-8e59-001430a5ac43', '157573de-e4fd-418b-9e2b-b4772e5fe137', 'b2e3d430-7699-4dac-9f55-e84c5cd5ce9b', 'a-level', '1.4', '9702 coursebook 1.4 · Displacement–time graphs', 34, 34, 'A curved s–t graph has a tangent of gradient 8.0 m s⁻¹ at 3.0 s and 12 m s⁻¹ at 5.0 s. What does this show?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The object is accelerating', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Velocity increases from 8.0 to 12 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: tangent gradients. C1: velocity increasing. A1: A (The object is accelerating).', 3, NULL, NULL),
