('646657e8-3051-5df8-8a2f-adedb90c4e80', '157573de-e4fd-418b-9e2b-b4772e5fe137', 'b2e3d430-7699-4dac-9f55-e84c5cd5ce9b', 'a-level', '1.4', '9702 coursebook 1.4 · Displacement–time graphs', 40, 40, 'For a car whose s–t graph rises from 300 m at 20 s to 700 m at 60 s in a straight line, calculate its velocity in that interval.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '10', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = (700 − 300) ÷ (60 − 20) = 10 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: Δs. C1: Δt. A1: v = 10 m s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('a1c54d5e-13cd-5dab-b30e-e3d6df4e7fef', '157573de-e4fd-418b-9e2b-b4772e5fe137', 'b2e3d430-7699-4dac-9f55-e84c5cd5ce9b', 'a-level', '1.4', '9702 coursebook 1.4 · Displacement–time graphs', 41, 41, 'A tangent to the s–t graph of a falling ball at t = 3.0 s passes through (2.0 s, 5.0 m) and (4.0 s, 64 m). Calculate the ball''s speed at 3.0 s.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '29.5', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = (64 − 5.0) ÷ (4.0 − 2.0) = 29.5 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: tangent gradient. C1: value. A1: v = 29.5 m s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('9111dfa3-a902-561c-8bec-166e5ff24d12', '157573de-e4fd-418b-9e2b-b4772e5fe137', 'b2e3d430-7699-4dac-9f55-e84c5cd5ce9b', 'a-level', '1.4', '9702 coursebook 1.4 · Displacement–time graphs', 42, 42, 'Car A starts at s = 0 at 20 m s⁻¹. Car B starts at s = 200 m at the same time and moves at 12 m s⁻¹ in the same direction. (a) Write s for each car in terms of t. (b) Calculate when their s–t lines cross.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '25', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) s_A = 20t; s_B = 200 + 12t. (b) 20t = 200 + 12t gives t = 200 ÷ 8 = 25 s. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: equations. M1: equate. C1: rearrange. C1: value. A1: t = 25 s.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgf7194584-t fgf7194584-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgf7194584-t">Two cars</title><desc id="fgf7194584-d">Displacement–time lines for car A (from 0 at 20 m s⁻¹) and car B (from 200 m at 12 m s⁻¹).</desc><line x1="36.2" y1="34" x2="36.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="122.6" y1="34" x2="122.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="209.1" y1="34" x2="209.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="295.5" y1="34" x2="295.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="36.2" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="36.2" y