('005f6a23-4f32-541a-bbfa-509d3df3e5cd', '157573de-e4fd-418b-9e2b-b4772e5fe137', 'b2e3d430-7699-4dac-9f55-e84c5cd5ce9b', 'a-level', '1.4', '9702 coursebook 1.4 · Displacement–time graphs', 43, 43, 'An object has s = 5.0t − t² (s in m, t in s). (a) Calculate s at t = 1.0 s and t = 4.0 s. (b) Find when its s–t graph is at a maximum. (c) Calculate the maximum displacement.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '6.25', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) s(1.0) = 4.0 m; s(4.0) = 4.0 m. (b) By symmetry the maximum is midway: t = (1.0 + 4.0) ÷ 2 = 2.5 s. (c) s = 5.0 × 2.5 − 2.5² = 6.25 m. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: s values. M1: symmetry or zero gradient. C1: t = 2.5 s. M1: substitute. C1: value. A1: s_max = 6.25 m.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg93cff8c0-t fg93cff8c0-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg93cff8c0-t">s = 5.0t − t²</title><desc id="fg93cff8c0-d">The curve s = 5.0t − t² from 0 to 5.0 s: it rises, reaches a maximum and falls back to zero.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="95.6" y1="34" x2="95.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="167.2" y1="34" x2="167.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="238.8" y1="34" x2="238.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="310.4" y1="34" x2="310.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width: