('d0162729-445b-57bb-adfc-ebb99f97115a', '157573de-e4fd-418b-9e2b-b4772e5fe137', 'b2e3d430-7699-4dac-9f55-e84c5cd5ce9b', 'a-level', '1.4', '9702 coursebook 1.4 · Displacement–time graphs', 48, 48, 'A cyclist rides at constant velocity and is at 80 m at t = 4.0 s and 200 m at t = 12 s. (a) Calculate her velocity. (b) Calculate her displacement at t = 0. (c) Calculate when she passes 300 m.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '18.67', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) v = 120 ÷ 8.0 = 15 m s⁻¹. (b) s₀ = 80 − 15 × 4.0 = 20 m. (c) t = (300 − 20) ÷ 15 = 18.7 s. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: velocity. C1: s₀. M1: rearrange s = s₀ + vt. C1: value. A1: t = 18.7 s.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fge13fb6a0-t fge13fb6a0-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fge13fb6a0-t">Cyclist displacement–time graph</title><desc id="fge13fb6a0-d">A straight s–t line through (4.0 s, 80 m) and (12 s, 200 m).</desc><line x1="36.2" y1="34" x2="36.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="105.3" y1="34" x2="105.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="174.5" y1="34" x2="174.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="243.7" y1="34" x2="243.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="312.8" y1="34" x2="312.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><lin